<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sawayama Castle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sawayama Castle was a Japanese mountain castle on Mount Sawa, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hikone">Hikone</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiga-prefecture">Shiga Prefecture</a>, commanding the road along the eastern side of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-biwa">Lake Biwa</a>. It was the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishida-mitsunari">Ishida Mitsunari</a> until it fell to Tokugawa forces after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Battle of Sekigahara</a> in 1600. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ii-naomasa">Ii Naomasa</a> held it briefly, and its materials were reused for the new Hikone Castle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sawayama-castle.jpg" alt="Sawayama Castle" width="320" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 投稿者がファイル作成 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sawayama-jyo01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
